WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.130
Remote working has been around for
some time but has become essential

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.480
for many businesses over the last
year or so due to the pandemic and

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.019
looks like continuing trend for many
companies for the foreseeable future.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.619
This means that cyber security has
become of greater concern for businesses.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:23.860
Rigorous and powerful cybersecurity
is needed to protect employees working

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:29.279
remotely such as VPN or investing
in the more secure zero trust model.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.379
In a world where employees could be
working from many places such as at home,

00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:39.790
a coffee shop, or on holiday; zero trust
works on the principle of don’t trust

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.510
by default and uses additional factors
to assess whether to grant access.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.060
These could be where is
the user signing in from?

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.010
What time are they signing in?

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:54.909
Is this a normal time when they
usually sign in between 9am and 5pm?

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.030
What device are they accessing from?

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.550
And many other potential factors that
could indicate a risky sign-in attempt.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.440
On site security is easier to handle
than using unsafe WiFi networks.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.390
When using untrusted WiFi networks,
employees should be sure to use

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.690
a corporate VPN so that their
connection is encrypted end-to-end.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.650
We must also be aware of human error along
with other vulnerabilities such as weak

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.590
password or the use of the same password.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.179
Working should always take place in safe
environments, so as not to have security

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.239
impacted by having others present.

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:36.910
That's why it’s not ideal to work on a
train, in a cafe or in a hotel or business

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:41.150
reception or even in the park, where
others can see important information

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.549
and security cannot be guaranteed.

00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:49.250
Whilst working in public, employees should
be wary of shoulder-surfing that people

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.700
can’t view any potentially sensitive
data that they may have on screen.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.589
Privacy screens can be used which blur
the screen of anyone who is not sat

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.170
directly in front of the computer.

